\subsection{Noise-free mismatch floor}
\label{sec:model-mismatch-ablation}
Replaying the records with sensor corruption disabled while retaining the estimators' ordinary covariances,
regularization, adaptation, and startup isolates a \emph{deployed-estimator}
residual, not pure plant-model mismatch. Eight equal-length stationary records
are pooled over their final \SI{900}{s}.

OU--III vertical and 3-D RMS are $0.145$ and $0.312$~m, versus $0.249$ and
$0.440$~m for OU--II and $0.145$ and $0.315$~m for TFG
(Fig.~\ref{fig:model-mismatch-floor}). Nonzero estimated bias with zero
true bias demonstrates absorption of model residuals.
Fig.~\ref{fig:model-mismatch-scaling}
shows near-proportional residual growth over the prescribed seas; its
slope-one line is a reference, not a fitted law. Incident $H_s$ is not the
vessel's heave height.
\begin{table}[t]
  \centering
  \caption{Noise-free deployed-estimator mismatch floor over eight stationary
  records.  $Z/Z_{\rm ref}$ is normalized by pooled reference vertical RMS.}
  \label{tab:model-mismatch-floor}
  \footnotesize
  \setlength{\tabcolsep}{3.4pt}
  \begin{tabular}{@{}lrrrrr@{}}
    \toprule
    Family & $X$ [m] & $Y$ [m] & $Z$ [m] & 3-D [m] & $Z/Z_{\rm ref}$ [\%] \\
    \midrule
    OU--II & 0.308 & 0.192 & 0.249 & 0.440 & 20.46 \\
    OU--III & 0.240 & 0.136 & 0.145 & 0.312 & 11.89 \\
    TFG & 0.234 & 0.153 & 0.145 & 0.315 & 11.95 \\
    \bottomrule
  \end{tabular}
\end{table}

